#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c6edbe-0d21-5292-af54-3aee476000ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342310} {:answer/id #uuid "93a81b6f-340c-5a38-93ca-46a5ff16f29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342311} {:answer/id #uuid "2383bcff-b9da-593f-88c2-e89a2f61299a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342312} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca59082-0a28-52be-80e6-2e8a54550b5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342313} {:answer/id #uuid "8a29d6a2-873c-5695-b181-655cccae2a0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15c6edbe-0d21-5292-af54-3aee476000ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342310} :answer-field/id #uuid "40a81efe-bb81-5712-8a60-556d0e16bd14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ba1202f-23bb-59b7-8a58-51ad745d9aba" :question/math-academy-id "q-15225" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/6c70d5f15424c4d7d67a3998a785a214e46e8dfa47b83839fd99a574b2f756cf.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-1,6]$, is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(4,0)$ with radius $1.$ Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[0,5].$" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-0}\\cdot (3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6441432-c33b-55f9-8ad3-ece97b055c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6441432-c33b-55f9-8ad3-ece97b055c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342321} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cdfcd64-e975-5f9a-a87e-656249c63b24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f43cc69-bbf5-5e06-8e03-26d2b66ad73a" :question/math-academy-id "q-344702" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/8ddd8493662174e0ddaf9bdd63b0ec382f6bb25c9079f1a339b71400b8cf3860.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-6,6],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $15$, $60$ and $9,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-6,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-15+60-9=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-6)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
